,"action":"main","from":"Buy","to":"Buy"}]},"profile":{"sector":"Technology","industry":"Software - Application","summary":"Automatic Data Processing, Inc. provides cloud-based human capital management (HCM) solutions worldwide. It operates in two segments, Employer Services and Professional Employer Organization (PEO). The Employer Services segment offers strategic, cloud-based platforms, and human resources (HR) outsourcing solutions. This segment's offerings include RUN Powered by ADP, a software platform for small business payroll, HR, and compliance; ADP Workforce Now, a HCM solution used across mid-sized and large businesses to manage employees; and ADP Lyric HCM, a solution for HR management, payroll, workforce management, talent, and data analytics. Its PEO Services segment provides HR outsourcing solutions under ADP TotalSource name to businesses through a co-employment model. This segment also provides guidance, user-friendly technology, comprehensive employee benefits, and a risk management, safety, and workers' compensation program. The company was founded in 1949 and is headquartered in Roseland, New Jersey.","employees":67000,"website":"https://www.adp.com","country":"United States","city":"Roseland","officers":[{"name":"Ms. Maria  Black","title":"President, CEO & DIrector"},{"name":"Mr. Peter J. Hadley","title":"Chief Financial Officer"},{"name":"Mr. Joseph  DeSilva Jr.","title":"Executive VP of North America & Chief of Operations"}]},"sector_medians":{"fpe":18.39,"tpe":32.55,"ps":6.516,"pfcf":32.14,"peg":1.005,"pb":7.933,"rev_growth":0.215,"eps_growth":0.4515,"eps_growth_fwd":0.2552,"eps_growth_next":0.1933,"div_yield":0.0011,"roe":0.2323,"roa":0.07977,"de":47.91,"gross_margin":0.5924,"op_margin":0.225,"profit_margin":0.1914,"current_ratio":1.554},"valuation":[{"k":"fpe","label":"Forward P/E","v":22.69,"sector":18.39,"verdict":"Fairly valued"},{"k":"tpe","label":"TTM P/E","v":27.8,"sector":32.55,"verdict":"Fairly valued"},{"k":"ps","label":"Price / S